  const takeScreenshotButton = document.getElementById("take-screenshot");
  takeScreenshotButton.addEventListener("click", function () {
    chrome.tabs.query({ active: true, currentWindow: true }, function (tabs) {
      chrome.tabs.sendMessage(tabs[0].id, { action: "take-screenshot" });
    });
  });
});
```
**contentScript.js**
```javascript
chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener(function (request, sender, sendResponse) {
  if (request.action === "take-screenshot") {
    chrome.tabs.captureVisibleTab(null, { format: "png" }, function (dataUrl) {
      const screenshot = new Blob([dataUrl], { type: "image/png" });
      const link = document.createElement("a");
      link.href = URL.createObjectURL(screenshot);
      link.download = "screenshot.png";
      link.click();
    });
  }
});
```
**How it works:**

1. The user clicks the "Take Screenshot" button in the popup.
2. The popup script sends a message to the content script to take a screenshot.
3. The content script uses the `chrome.tabs.captureVisibleTab` method to capture a screenshot of the current tab.
4. The content script creates a new blob with the screenshot data and creates a link to download the screenshot.
5. The content script clicks the link to download the screenshot.

